# LeakSanitizer suppressions.
#
# The .NET runtime allocates in ways LSAN reports as leaks but which we neither own nor control:
# the JIT, the GC's own bookkeeping, the host's startup allocations, and the system libraries
# the runtime links. Reporting those would bury the leaks that are actually ours.
#
# Nothing here suppresses a frame from libada or from this library's interop. If a leak in either
# is ever suppressed by one of these patterns, the pattern is wrong and should be narrowed.

# Everything the .NET host ships: the runtime, the JIT, the host, and every BCL assembly. libada
# and the interop are never loaded from here, so this cannot hide one of our leaks.
leak:/usr/share/dotnet/

# System libraries the host links. Basenames only, and none of them is the library under test.
leak:libc.so
leak:libcrypto
leak:libssl
leak:libicu
